{"ts":1781440816,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(plugin_mailbox_no_reentrant_host_fn, architecture, 'No host function exposed to WASM guests may invoke a path that reaches PluginHostPort::on_file_indexed/on_file_changed: the worker thread is the single consumer of its own bounded mailbox, so re-entering fan_out from inside a hook handler would block the worker on a send to its own full mailbox and self-deadlock. Today this holds only because all host functions (host_read_file, host_list_files, ast_store_get/put, host_log) are read-only or non-reentrant; adding any file-mutating host function reintroduces the hazard.', high, 'feat/internal-plugin-queue design+review 2026-06')"}
{"ts":1781440817,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(plugin_mailbox_no_reentrant_host_fn, 'crates/core_engine/src/adapters/plugin/loader.rs', directory)"}
{"ts":1781440820,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(plugin_registry_no_write_on_serving_path, architecture, 'No MCP-serving code path may take a write() guard on the Arc<RwLock<PluginHostRegistry>>. Watcher hook delivery (SharedPluginHost::on_file_*) does a blocking backpressuring mailbox send while holding the registry RwLock read guard; this never starves MCP only because every hot-path consumer (declared_tools, call_instance_tool, hooks) is also a reader and RwLock permits concurrent readers. A write() on a serving path would be blocked by watcher backpressure. register() is the only writer and runs at startup before the Arc<RwLock> is shared.', high, 'feat/internal-plugin-queue design+review 2026-06')"}
{"ts":1781440821,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(plugin_registry_no_write_on_serving_path, 'crates/core_engine/src/domain/plugin_host', directory)"}
{"ts":1781444546,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(mcp_mutations_use_real_plugin_host, architecture, 'MCP file-mutation handlers (create/delete/global_replace in adapters/mcp/native_tools.rs) MUST construct FileMutationService with the real plugin host, not NoOpPluginHost. The filesystem watcher cannot compensate: the MCP handler already mutated the shared VFS, so the watcher event hits an idempotent early-return (handle_create/handle_delete) and never fires the hook. Symptom when violated: deleted file symbols persist in the AST index forever (index-as-you-go cannot self-heal a deletion).', high, 'feat/internal-plugin-queue BUG1 fix a80f205 2026-06')"}
{"ts":1781444549,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(reconcile_persisted_index_on_startup, architecture, 'On normal boot (scan already complete) the persisted sled (workspace,index) is loaded verbatim; it MUST be reconciled against the current filesystem or stale entries become permanent ghosts (files deleted while the server was down, indexed by older code, or foreign atomic-save temps). Fix in scan::reconcile_pruned: path-only ignore-aware walk, drop tracked entries absent from the walk. Do NOT re-read/hash file contents (perf on large repos). Empirically: wiping .tower/db and rebuilding removed all ghosts, confirming load-verbatim as the cause.', high, 'feat/internal-plugin-queue BUG2 fix d76604d 2026-06')"}
{"ts":1781700896,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(bench_fsync_use_real_disk, pitfall, 'When benchmarking fsync or write durability, do NOT use the default tempdir: /tmp is tmpfs (RAM) so fsync is near-free and numbers are ~100x too fast. Force TMPDIR onto a real disk (e.g. under $HOME on NVMe/btrfs) before measuring', high, f3_ast_persist_benchmark)"}
{"ts":1781700896,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(bench_fsync_use_real_disk, 'benchmark', project)"}
{"ts":1781733605,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(lsp_e2e_retry_transient, test, 'Real-rust-analyzer e2e warm-up retry loops must treat a transient backend error (REQUEST_BUDGET timeout under parallel test load) as not-ready and retry, not panic via .expect(); re-raise only on the final attempt.', high, 'spec18-followup')"}
{"ts":1781733608,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(lsp_e2e_retry_transient, 'lsp_rust_analyzer_e2e', file)"}
{"ts":1781734701,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(cas_guard_fail_closed, pitfall, 'A CAS/precondition guard parsed from untrusted JSON must fail closed: a present-but-malformed expected_version (non-string) or expected_versions (non-object / non-string value) must be rejected with InvalidArgs, never silently dropped to an unconditional write - silent degradation defeats the safety property the guard exists to provide.', high, 'spec18-review')"}
{"ts":1781734704,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(cas_guard_fail_closed, 'native_tools', file)"}
{"ts":1781861765,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(sidecar_hostcall_before_init, pitfall, 'Sidecar extensions MUST perform all initialize-time HostCalls before sending Initialized; sending Initialized first lets the host send the next request while the extension is still in read_host_response, which silently discards non-matching-id frames and deadlocks', high, bug_2_commit_628a284)"}
{"ts":1781861765,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(sidecar_hostcall_before_init, 'extensions/', directory)"}
{"ts":1781861765,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(sidecar_read_host_response_discards, pitfall, 'read_host_response in extension protocol silently discards frames whose id does not match the awaited capability reply; an inbound host request arriving during a capability round-trip is lost -> deadlock. Long-lived/async extensions (LSP, spec 27) must queue inbound requests, not drop them', high, bug_2_commit_628a284)"}
{"ts":1781861765,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(sidecar_shutdown_kill_before_join, pitfall, 'SidecarHostAdapter::shutdown must escalate SIGTERM/SIGKILL BEFORE joining the reader thread; joining first deadlocks if the child does not voluntarily close stdout', high, bug_1_commit_628a284)"}
{"ts":1782206430,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(list_dir_mcp_missing_prefix_coverage, test, 'MCP integration coverage for tower_list_dir must include a missing/untracked prefix and assert a successful empty entries array, not an error.', medium, 'F001 T008 review remediation 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782207375,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(list_dir_no_doc_count_literals, test, 'When stabilizing the native MCP tool surface, source-scan tests must reject rustdoc examples that duplicate the native tool count, including assert_eq!(tools.len(), N) patterns.', medium, 'F001 T009 remediation 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782208045,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(native_tool_docs_sync, 'native tool docs', project)"}
{"ts":1782208045,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(native_tool_docs_sync, review, 'Update README quick-start examples, docs/getting-started.md, and docs/mcp-tools.md together whenever a native tower_* MCP tool is added or removed.', medium, 'F001 docs update 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782211662,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(watcher_delete_events_not_dropped, pitfall, 'Watcher filesystem events that affect index correctness, especially Delete, must not be dropped under extension or formatter backpressure; dropping Delete creates stale indexed ghosts until reindex or restart reconciliation.', high, 'test2.md stale index bug 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782211662,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(watcher_delete_uses_file_deleted, architecture, 'Watcher Delete handling must call ExtensionHostPort::on_file_deleted, not on_file_changed; fileChanged subscribers such as fmt must not receive deletion events for removed paths.', high, 'test2.md stale index bug 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782211941,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(watcher_modify_missing_path_deletes, pitfall, 'Watcher Modify handling must treat a tracked path that no longer exists on disk as Delete; some OS/editor paths report deletion as Modify/rename-like events, and default metadata would otherwise keep a stale index entry.', high, 'test3.md stale index bug 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782215827,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(f002_task_contract_names, review, 'Task acceptance criteria must name every public function type DTO and stable error code introduced or modified so implementers do not invent contracts later.', high, 'F002 PM Review 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782215828,"op":"assert","clause":"trigger(f002_task_contract_names, '.specify/implementation/*/tasks/*.md', file)"}
{"ts":1782219879,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(lint_parser_relative_path_escape, pitfall, 'Lint parser path normalization must reject relative diagnostic paths whose parent components would escape the supplied workspace_root, including when workspace_root is relative like .', high, 'F002 T012 review remediation 2026-06-23')"}
{"ts":1782221081,"op":"assert","clause":"rule(lint_runner_stdin_timeout_supervision, pitfall, 'Lint runner stdin writes must be supervised by the same timeout path as process waiting; never write large stdin synchronously before timeout supervision starts.', high, 'F002 T013 review remediation 2026-06-23')"}
